    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), both of whom benefit immensely from high-scoring matchups against vulnerable arms. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is our premier utility play, anchored by a +16% park factor and a favorable matchup against Bassitt, while **Gunnar Henderson** occupies the primary MI spot with a massive ceiling thanks to an elite environment against Van Eyk. Alongside them, **Kyle Tucker** (75.20) and **Drake Baldwin** (72.21) provide a high-floor foundation, with **Drake Baldwin** capitalizing on a leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Abbott. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.43) remains a must-start, as his dynamic platoon edge against Englert boosts him well into the strong category.\n\nWhile **Coby Mayo** (66.09) and **Andy Pages** (65.17) offer solid production, our bench decisions were dictated by the necessity of prioritizing efficiency as we approach our game caps. **Wade Meckler** (53.83) was the toughest exclusion; despite his high park and skill adjustments, the platoon disadvantage against Springs ultimately suppressed his efficiency rating below the required threshold for our active lineup. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (52.99) carries significant pedigree, but the tough matchup against Yamamoto forces him to the bench in favor of more efficient platoon-advantaged bats. We are monitoring the lineup status of **Nasim Nunez** (59.23); while his score is bolstered by his speed profile against a slow-delivery pitcher like Valdez, his #9 position remains a drag on his overall output. Investors should note that while **Henry Bolte** (59.23) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) provide necessary speed, the volatility of their respective matchups requires careful monitoring for mid-game defensive replacements.",
